 "market_view": "A weak US September payrolls print (+29k vs ~90k expected, unemployment 4.2%) cut Fed hike odds and lifted the S&P 500 0.7% and Nasdaq 1.2% on Friday, but the S&P still ended the week 0.3% lower with the US 10-year near 5.28%. The rand weakened 2.2% over the week to R16.66/$ and the JSE All Share fell 2.2% (Top 40 -2.3%) after the SARB raised the repo rate 25bp to 7.25% to lean against fuel-driven inflation (CPI 4.4% in August). Gold (-3.7%) and platinum (-5.1%) fell on the week while Brent held above $100/bbl; US yields above 5% remain the main valuation headwind for long-duration tech.",
